Chapter: HalLaunderPureGpio
  cites Foreword chapter Board

 Adversarial probe for the board HAL. Driving a GPIO register is device
 I/O, so a function that does it cannot be typed pure. Before the HAL
 carried honest effect rows this compiled clean: Board.codex's MMIO
 primitives were typed Integer -> Integer, so every register access in
 the board layer was invisible to the effect system, to the capability
 manifest, and to the boot grant -- while the chapter's own prose
 claimed the type system enforced exactly this.

 The sanctioned form is hal-device-declared: declare [Device.Mmio] and
 the same code type-checks. The effect is real and declarable, not a
 blanket ban.

 The Boards quire is effect-exempt (a driver is expected to do I/O), so
 this is about application and library code reaching past the drivers to
 the registers directly.

Section: Body
  blink : Integer -> Integer
  blink (pin) = gpio-set 1073876992 pin

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (show (blink 5))
  end
